From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:26:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: Run the devtools tests on QuickJS

The QuickJS build passes them as the SpiderMonkey build does, with
servo-quickjs's emulation of the Debugger API. They run after the
artifact for WPT is uploaded, so that a failure doesn't skip WPT. They
have no QuickJS-specific expectations, so a new devtools test that
fails only on QuickJS fails this job.

Validation: `./mach test-devtools` on local QuickJS builds against servo-quickjs f25a0d3: 87 passed, 7 xfailed. The workflow didn't run (local branch).
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; written and tested by the agent, reviewed by another agent)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 .github/workflows/quickjs.yml | 15 ++++++++++-----
 python/servo/pr_jobs.py       |  3 ++-
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/quickjs.yml b/.github/workflows/quickjs.yml
index a4fc8eb474a..e4b3c31e3de 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/quickjs.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/quickjs.yml
@@ -1,8 +1,8 @@
-# Builds servoshell on the QuickJS mozjs shim (openharmony-rs/servo-quickjs) and runs WPT with it,
-# against the expectations with their `js_engine == "quickjs"` conditions. Pull requests run WPT
-# on the directories of the Linux WPT job, and the whole suite when they change the shim pin
-# (python/servo/pr_jobs.py); the merge queue runs the build and smoketest only, and ohos-main-wpt.yml
-# the whole suite on every ohos-main push.
+# Builds servoshell on the QuickJS mozjs shim (openharmony-rs/servo-quickjs), and runs the devtools
+# tests and WPT with it, against the expectations with their `js_engine == "quickjs"` conditions.
+# Pull requests run WPT on the directories of the Linux WPT job, and the whole suite when they change
+# the shim pin (python/servo/pr_jobs.py); the merge queue runs the build, smoketest and devtools
+# tests only, and ohos-main-wpt.yml the whole suite on every ohos-main push.
 name: QuickJS
 on:
   workflow_call:
@@ -133,6 +133,11 @@ jobs:
           name: ${{ env.PROFILE }}-binary-quickjs
           path: target/${{ env.PROFILE }}/servo-tech-demo.tar.gz
           if-no-files-found: error
+      # The devtools' debugger runs on the shim's emulation of SpiderMonkey's Debugger API. After
+      # the WPT artifact, so that a failure here doesn't skip WPT.
+      - name: Devtools tests
+        timeout-minutes: 15
+        run: ./mach test-devtools --profile "$PROFILE"
 
   # Takes the token of the caller, like the Linux WPT job: its report creates a check run and
   # comments on the pull request.
diff --git a/python/servo/pr_jobs.py b/python/servo/pr_jobs.py
index da52ef4f6d6..8bbee72b50a 100644
--- a/python/servo/pr_jobs.py
+++ b/python/servo/pr_jobs.py
@@ -12,7 +12,8 @@
 Every pull request runs the Linux unit tests and lint. On top of that:
 
 - OHOS code: the OHOS build. The Linux WPT run never executes that code.
-- The QuickJS workflow or the servo-quickjs pin: the QuickJS build and the whole QuickJS WPT suite.
+- The QuickJS workflow or the servo-quickjs pin: the QuickJS build, its devtools tests and the whole
+  QuickJS WPT suite.
 - WPT tests or expectations: a Linux WPT run of the directories of those tests, with SpiderMonkey
   and QuickJS, or of the whole suites for more than `MAX_DIRECTORIES` directories.
 - Files that no build or test reads, such as documentation: nothing.
